<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  OWASP Dependency-Check suppressions (Phase 31).

  A suppression is a DECISION, so each one records why and until when:

    <notes>      why this finding is not a risk here, or why it cannot be fixed yet
    until=       an expiry date; after it, the finding fails the build again and has to be
                 looked at afresh. There are no permanent suppressions.

  Fix first (upgrade, or override the managed version in the root pom); suppress only a false
  positive (the CPE matched the wrong product) or a vulnerability in code this project provably
  does not reach. docs/security.md lists every finding and what was done about it.

  Empty until a finding needs one.
-->
<suppressions xmlns="https://jeremylong.github.io/DependencyCheck/dependency-suppression.1.3.xsd">
</suppressions>
